  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Mar 2025 13th St (south frontage): low one-storey flat-roofed building, cream/white walls under pale blue fascia panels, a glazed central double-door entrance; a darker olive wing with brown trim to the west.",
    "inferred": "Window cadence, the olive treatment on the WSW-facing faces, doors on every side; north, courtyard and re-entrant sides are unseen.",
    "footprint": "Frozen relation r133351: outer ring (61 edges) kept as one block around its inner courtyard ring.",
    "grid_b5": "Mar 2025 photos (r133351-sideD_240 and 883-sideB_153): the olive wing's WSW wall at e4 is windowless (round logo only)",
    "wholeunit": "Mar 2025 r133351-sideD_240 (pano zHJe3vjFyKW1aAgqgdeypw, h 48): the e4 bump is a tall dark slate box (about 5.6 m to the fascia top) with a deep overhanging fascia about 1 m tall; its fascia ends match the OSM outline, so the walls sit about 1.2 m inside it on the WSW and 1.25 m in from both ends. Box depth (20 m), the SSE door and the roof are inference.",
    "wholeunit_ends": "The ends under the gym overhang differ on purpose, following sideD_240: at the NW end the photo shows a lower pale porch/hall under the fascia, so hall_nw fills the 1.25 m strip at hall height; at the SE end the photo shows an open dark pocket under the fascia (equipment, fence), so that strip stays open ground."
